From the source code, I figured out the following:
Luck is secondary to what happens when you sit on a throne:
First, the game determines whether anything at all happens.  (If nothing,
you get the "..out of place" message).  This is purely random and something
will happen about 1 in 6 tries, regardless of luck.
Next, if something does happen the game decides what.  Again, purely random
(not based on luck at all).  There are 13 different things, some good, some
bad.  One of the possibilities is getting a wish if your luck is high enough.
(If it isn't, it boosts your luck by 1 instead).
Lastly, the game decides (purely randomly) if the throne vanishes or not.

With unicorns, a far easier way to boost luck is to throw an unidentified
gem at any unicorn (similar alignment or not).  This should boost your
luck by 1 whether the gem is real or fake.

